actual game.)

...but, OTOH, my games vary a lot; in some games Rodney re-appeared
just twice (or so) and in other games he appears 15 (or more) times.
In some games I am affected by the force 40 times (even as chaotic)
and I had played a lawful character that was thrown back just twice.
Considering all that randomness, speedy play is, while important, not
that significant a factor compared to the above mentioned; you have to
win your game in any case, with or without delay, with many or with
few force effects, with a lot resurrections, double troubles, nasties
summoning, or with less of those.

If one is able to reach thus far - and some say that once in Gehennom
the game is solved - being speedy reduces the number of nuisances but
doesn't impose any real problem (as long as there's no accumulated
amount of bad luck and/or bad or inattentive play involved). Though,
for first-ascenders it's certainly more important to be well prepared
and to not delay the ascension run.

